<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05JU">Definition <span data-tag="05JU">8.6.6.7</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets, so that the induced map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \lambda : \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}} \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}} \]
</div>
<p> is a left fibration (Proposition <a data-tag="03JT" href="/tag/03JT">8.1.1.15</a>). Let $\kappa $ be an uncountable cardinal. We say that a diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathscr {H}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}} \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt;\kappa } \]
</div>
<p> is a <em>relative $\operatorname{Hom}$-functor for $U$</em> if it is a covariant transport representation for the left fibration $\lambda $ (Definition <a data-tag="028V" href="/tag/028V">5.6.5.1</a>). </p>
</article>
